## 3. Model Selection (Optimized for Colab Free Tier — 15 GB VRAM T4)

### 3.1 Client-Side Models (Browser — runs via ONNX Runtime Web + WebGPU)

| Role | Model | Size | Latency | Why This Model |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Face Detection** | BlazeFace (MediaPipe) | ~400 KB | <10 ms | Fastest browser face detector; real-time; sub-ms on WebGPU |
| **Text PII (NER)** | Xenova/bert-base-NER (quantized INT8 ONNX) | ~65 MB | ~50 ms | Proven browser NER; runs in Web Worker; detects PERSON, ORG, LOC |
| **Screen Understanding** | MobileViT-XXS (ONNX q8) | ~5 MB | ~30 ms | Lightweight ViT for screen classification; WebGPU accelerated |
| **OCR (on-device)** | Tesseract.js (WASM) | ~15 MB | ~200 ms | Extract text from screenshots locally for PII scanning |
| **Regex PII** | Custom regex engine | ~2 KB | <1 ms | Deterministic: emails, phones, Aadhaar, PAN, credit cards, passwords |

> [!TIP]
> **Hybrid PII Strategy**: Regex catches structured PII (100% precision), NER catches contextual PII (names, addresses), BlazeFace catches faces, OCR catches text-in-images. This 4-layer defense maximizes the 20% recall/precision score.

### 3.2 Server-Side Models (Colab Free Tier — T4 16 GB VRAM)

We run **two separate Colab notebooks** — one for LLM, one for VLM — exposed via ngrok tunnels:

| Role | Model | Quantization | VRAM Usage | Why This Model |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **LLM (Planner/Reasoner)** | **Qwen3-14B** (4-bit AWQ) | Q4_K_M | ~10 GB | Best reasoning at 14B; strong CoT; agentic tool-use; structured JSON output |
| **VLM (Visual Grounding)** | **Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct** (4-bit BnB) | INT4 | ~6 GB | SOTA GUI grounding; bounding box prediction; action prediction from screenshots |

> [!WARNING]
> **T4 Limitation**: T4 lacks Flash Attention 2 (needs Ampere+). Disable it in config. Use `load_in_4bit=True` via bitsandbytes. Resize screenshots to max 1280px width before VLM inference.

**Alternative Models** (if Colab upgrades or you get better GPU):

| Model | Use Case | VRAM |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Qwen3-30B-A3B (MoE) | Better reasoning, same VRAM as 14B | ~12 GB Q4 |
| Gemma-4-12B | Strong multimodal alternative | ~8 GB Q4 |
| DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B | Step-by-step chain-of-thought | ~10 GB Q4 |

