### Layer 4: Privacy Engine (Sanitization Pipeline)

This is the **critical differentiator** — the 4-stage privacy pipeline:

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Stage 1: Visual PII Detection"
        IMG["Screenshot"] --> FACE["BlazeFace → Face BBs"]
        IMG --> OCR["Tesseract.js → Extract Text"]
        OCR --> NER["BERT-NER → Named Entities"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Stage 2: DOM PII Detection"
        DOM["DOM Snapshot"] --> REGEX["Regex Engine"]
        DOM --> DOMNER["BERT-NER on text nodes"]
        REGEX --> R1["Emails, Phones, Aadhaar, PAN, Credit Cards"]
        DOMNER --> R2["Names, Addresses, Organizations"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Stage 3: Redaction"
        FACE --> REDACT["Redaction Engine"]
        R1 --> REDACT
        R2 --> REDACT
        NER --> REDACT
        REDACT --> REDACTED_IMG["Black-box faces + blur PII regions"]
        REDACT --> REDACTED_DOM["Replace PII with tokens:<br/>[NAME_1], [EMAIL_1], [PHONE_1]"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Stage 4: Redaction Map (Client-Only)"
        REDACT --> MAP["Redaction Map<br/>(never sent to server)"]
        MAP --> RESTORE["Used to restore data<br/>when executing actions"]
    end
```

**PII Categories Detected**:

| Category | Detection Method | Example → Redacted |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Faces | BlazeFace | Photo → Black rectangle |
| Names | BERT-NER | "Aditya Sharma" → `[NAME_1]` |
| Emails | Regex + NER | "aditya@gmail.com" → `[EMAIL_1]` |
| Phone Numbers | Regex | "+91 98765 43210" → `[PHONE_1]` |
| Aadhaar | Regex (pattern: XXXX XXXX XXXX) | "1234 5678 9012" → `[AADHAAR_1]` |
| PAN | Regex (ABCDE1234F) | "ABCPD1234E" → `[PAN_1]` |
| Credit Cards | Regex (Luhn) | "4111-1111-1111-1111" → `[CARD_1]` |
| Passwords | DOM `type="password"` | "••••••" → `[PASSWORD_FIELD]` |
| Addresses | BERT-NER (LOC) | "123 MG Road, Delhi" → `[ADDRESS_1]` |

**Redaction Map** (stays on client, never transmitted):
