### 6.3 Dynamic Obstacle Handling (Point 19)

```mermaid
graph TD
    STEP["Execute Step"] --> VERIFY["Verify Expected State"]
    VERIFY -->|"Match"| NEXT["Proceed to Next Step"]
    VERIFY -->|"Mismatch"| DETECT["Obstacle Detection"]
    
    DETECT --> CLASSIFY{"Classify Obstacle"}
    CLASSIFY -->|"Popup / Ad"| DISMISS["Find ✕ button → Click → Retry"]
    CLASSIFY -->|"Login Wall"| LOGIN["Check vault → Request approval → Login"]
    CLASSIFY -->|"CAPTCHA"| CAPTCHA["Pause → Notify user → Wait"]
    CLASSIFY -->|"Cookie Banner"| COOKIE["Accept/Dismiss → Retry"]
    CLASSIFY -->|"Page Change"| REPLAN["Send new DOM to server → Re-plan"]
    CLASSIFY -->|"Unknown"| FALLBACK["Screenshot → Send to VLM → Get guidance"]
```

**Server-side obstacle prompt template**:
```
The agent expected to see [EXPECTED_STATE] but encountered an unexpected element.
Current DOM contains: [OBSTACLE_DOM_SNIPPET]
Screenshot attached.
Classify this obstacle and provide the appropriate action to resolve it.
Respond in structured JSON only.
```

